You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C01
Scenario title: Morning Preparation and Childcare Drop-off
Initial workflow description:
I get my child ready in the morning, pack what we need, and take them to childcare. If we are running late, I let someone know.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What specific time or signal tells you that you are 'running late' — for example, is there a target departure time or a childcare opening deadline you are measuring against?",
      "answer": "The workflow references an 'arrival window' checked at the start of the routine. Whether the escort can meet that arrival window is the explicit trigger for determining lateness. The specific clock time of that window is not specified in the available information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "When you need to notify someone that you are running late, who do you contact and through what channel or system — for example, a phone call, a messaging app, or a childcare centre portal?",
      "answer": "An arrival delay notice is sent to the childcare teacher via a childcare messaging app. The notice is drafted for the parent's confirmation before sending. No other contact or channel is specified for delay notifications."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "Can you list the individual tasks involved in getting your child ready and packing — for example, preparing food, locating items, dressing — so we understand the full set of manual steps?",
      "answer": "The documented packing steps are: reviewing the daily item list, packing and checking the bag, and resolving any missing items before departure. Specific sub-tasks such as preparing food or dressing are not individually listed in the available information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "Is there a sign-in, handover confirmation, or attendance record produced at drop-off, and if so, how is it captured?",
      "answer": "Yes. A handover confirmation is produced at drop-off. It is confirmed in person with the childcare teacher and recorded in an attendance register. The handover step remains in-person and is not automated."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "On which days of the week does this routine occur, and does the schedule vary — for example, different days in different weeks?",
      "answer": "The routine occurs on weekday mornings. Whether it occurs on all five weekdays or varies across weeks is not specified in the available information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What do you do if an unexpected situation arises that prevents the normal drop-off — such as the childcare centre being closed or your child being unwell?",
      "answer": "The workflow identifies exceptions including an escort being unavailable, an arrival delay, and an unacknowledged handover. If the assigned escort cannot meet the arrival window, a backup caregiver is confirmed and the teacher is notified. Scenarios such as the centre being closed or the child being unwell are not specified."
    }
  ]
}
